omr-server (0.1077) unstable; urgency=medium

    * Update omr-admin to 0.18+20260906: add GET /mqvpn_users (admin only), listing each MQVPN user as configured in /etc/mqvpn/server.json (with its fixed_ip), known by the running daemon and currently connected, the three being able to differ since a user is persisted even when the live add_user call fails; the control socket address is now read from server.json's control_listen instead of a hardcoded 127.0.0.1:9090, and sessions authenticated with the server-wide key are counted in global_key_clients instead of being listed as users
    * Update omr-admin: fix POST /vxlan_user with force=true merging two users onto the same VNI while both kept the default UDP port 4789, which left the second user's omr-vxlan@ unit failing at ip link add with no tunnel at all (Linux refuses a second VXLAN device with the same VNI on the same dstport); /vxlan_user and /vxlan now take a port and reject a VNI+port pair already held by another user whatever force says, GET /vxlan_vnis lists the port next to the VNI, and vni (0-16777215) and port (1-65535) are range-checked
    * Update omr-admin: fix the userid-derived VXLAN L3 default addresses, 10.255.249.<userid*4+1>/30 overflowing past .255 from userid 64 on and fd00::b0<hex> growing a fifth hex digit from userid 256 on; userids 0-63 keep their 10.255.249.0/24 slice, 64-1087 continue into 10.255.224.0/20 and 256-4095 use fd00::b<hex>:x, and past those pools no default is derived and localip/localip6 must be set explicitly
    * Update omr-admin: fix install_omr-ai.sh failing at the admin token bootstrap on every fresh install with influxdb3-core 3.10/3.11 (https://github.com/Ysurac/openmptcprouter/issues/4366), honour RESET_DATA, INSTALL_AI and INFLUX_RETENTION* from the environment, and write /etc/influxdb3/omr-influxdb.env as soon as the token is created so a later failure cannot lose a token that is never shown again
    * Update mqvpn to 0.16.2: fix a heap use-after-free in the server, reachable by any authenticated client sending a second CONNECT-IP request on the same HTTP/3 connection (it overwrote the assigned IP and left a dangling session entry, also leaking an address-pool slot); a duplicate is now rejected with 409 while the tunnel stream is live, and the session is released when that stream closes and can be re-established on a fresh one
    * mqvpn control API now answers get_stats, get_status, get_build_info, get_fec_stats and get_reorder_stats in client mode instead of returning all-zero counters and an "unknown" scheduler
    * mqvpn no longer closes a healthy multipath connection when a single stream frame exceeds the reassembly cap: the frame is dropped unacked instead of escalating to FRAME_ENCODING_ERROR

